# --- line endings ---
# Normalise line endings to LF for every text file (the models are XML/SVG text; a CRLF
# checkout would otherwise show every line of a .bpmn as changed and break byte-stable
# diffs of the models). `text=auto` leaves files git detects as binary untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bpmn text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Controls the contents of the GitHub release source archive — and therefore the Zenodo deposit.
#
# GitHub builds the release tarball/zip with `git archive`, which honors `export-ignore`, and
# Zenodo archives that tarball. So the published/archived release is trimmed to the citable
# artifact — the BPMN models + their SVG images — plus the essential metadata, without the
# development & tooling scaffolding.
#
# KEPT in the archive: models/ (.bpmn + .svg + models/README.md), README.md, AI_USAGE.md, CHANGELOG.md
# (written by release-please on main and back-merged to dev), LICENSE, CITATION.cff,
# DISCLAIMER.md, and docs/governance/ (the acceptance-test instrument). Everything listed
# below is EXCLUDED — including .zenodo.json: Zenodo reads the deposit metadata from the
# repository via the GitHub API at release time, not from the archive.
#
# NOTE: applies to FUTURE releases only — the file must be present in the tagged commit. The
# already-published GitHub releases v0.2.0-rc.1 and v0.2.1-rc.1 are unaffected (untrimmed; only
# v0.2.1-rc.1 of the two is on Zenodo); v0.2.1-rc.2 onwards are trimmed. To exclude/keep more,
# edit the lists below.

# --- development & build tooling ---
/tools/                         export-ignore
/skills/                        export-ignore
/.github/                       export-ignore
/package.json                   export-ignore
/package-lock.json              export-ignore
/release-please-config.json     export-ignore
/.release-please-manifest.json  export-ignore
/version.txt                    export-ignore
/.bpmnlintrc                    export-ignore

# --- editor / agent / repo meta ---
/.claude/                       export-ignore
/.agents/                       export-ignore
/.gitignore                     export-ignore
/.gitattributes                 export-ignore
/.editorconfig                  export-ignore
/.mailmap                       export-ignore
/.nvmrc                         export-ignore
/SECURITY.md                    export-ignore
/.zenodo.json                   export-ignore
/AGENTS.md                      export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md                      export-ignore

# --- contributor & process docs (not part of the model artifact) ---
/CONTRIBUTING.md                export-ignore
/CONVENTIONS.md                 export-ignore
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md             export-ignore
# docs/governance/ (the acceptance-test instrument) is KEPT; the process docs are excluded:
/docs/decisions/                export-ignore
/docs/model-issues/             export-ignore
# Research / working notes at the docs ROOT (Synthea primer, dataset-generation plan, data
# sources for probabilities/timing) are not part of the citable artifact. `*` does not cross
# `/`, so this matches only docs/<file>.md — docs/governance/ stays KEPT.
/docs/*.md                      export-ignore
